                <pb facs="0832" n="1666" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1666"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/521</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-08T21:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 8, 1918, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 8, 4.26
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1053. Embassy’s 1052, February 7, 5 p.m. Upon learning yesterday of Lasteyrie’s
                    proposed departure, the King immediately sent <pb facs="0833" n="1667"
                        xml:id="pg1667"/> for him, and, according to French Ambassador, stated that
                    the United States was trying to force Spain to inject the shipping and tonnage
                    question into Spanish-American agreement; that if United States insisted, both
                    Spanish-American and French-Spanish negotiations were at an end; but that if,
                    however, this point was dropped by the United States he would do his best to
                    secure ratification of French-Spanish agreement and did not doubt but that he
                    would be successful.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
